//
// Window measured from `terminal_at`, not `reserved_at` (R-7.6): three years from the row's OWN
// terminal transition, never from the reserve that started it — a row still `reserved` cannot
// satisfy `terminal_at < cutoff` at all, because the table CHECK ties the two together
// (`data-model.md:1743`, `CHECK ((state = 'reserved') = (terminal_at IS NULL))`).
//
// Base64, bound as ONE `$1` parameter: `queryReplacement` is positional CSV, so a value holding a
// comma breaks it and an empty value silently shifts every later `$N`. Base64 has neither, and it is
// driver-bound rather than interpolated — the SQLi shape vdd-multi caught on the snapshotter.
